{"path":"numeric/complex/cexp","title":"cexpf, cexp, cexpl","titleHtml":"cexpf, cexp, cexpl","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/c/numeric/complex/cexp","section":"numeric","kind":"page","summary":"If no errors occur, e raised to the power of z, ez is returned.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex\"><code>&lt;complex.h&gt;</code></a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-c99\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">float</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/complex\"><span class=\"kw743\">complex</span></a> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; cexpf<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">float</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/complex\"><span class=\"kw743\">complex</span></a> z <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(since C99)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-c99\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">double</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/complex\"><span class=\"kw743\">complex</span></a> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;cexp<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/complex\"><span class=\"kw743\">complex</span></a> z <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(since C99)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-c99\" id=\"Version_3\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">long</span> <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/complex\"><span class=\"kw743\">complex</span></a> cexpl<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">long</span> <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/complex\"><span class=\"kw743\">complex</span></a> z <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (3) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(since C99)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/tgmath\"><code>&lt;tgmath.h&gt;</code></a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-c99\" id=\"Version_4\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"co2\">#define exp( z )</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (4) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(since C99)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1-3)</span> Computes the complex base-<i>e</i> exponential of <code>z</code>.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">4)</span> Type-generic macro: If <code>z</code> has type <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">long</span> <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/complex\"><span class=\"kw743\">complex</span></a></span></code>, <code>cexpl</code> is called. if <code>z</code> has type <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">double</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/complex\"><span class=\"kw743\">complex</span></a></span></code>, <code>cexp</code> is called, if <code>z</code> has type <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">float</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/complex\"><span class=\"kw743\">complex</span></a></span></code>, <code>cexpf</code> is called. If <code>z</code> is real or integer, then the macro invokes the corresponding real function (<code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">expf</span></code>, <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/math/exp\"><span class=\"kw657\">exp</span></a></span></code>, <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">expl</span></code>). If <code>z</code> is imaginary, the corresponding complex argument version is called.</div>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td>  z\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td>  complex argument\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>If no errors occur, <i>e</i> raised to the power of <code>z</code>, <span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"\\small e^z\">e<span class=\"t-su\">z<br></span></span> is returned.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Error_handling_and_special_values\">Error handling and special values</h3>\n<p>Errors are reported consistent with <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/math/math_errhandling\"><code>math_errhandling</code></a>.\n</p><p>If the implementation supports IEEE floating-point arithmetic,\n</p>\n<ul><li> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">cexp<span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/conj\"><span class=\"kw760\">conj</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/conj\"><span class=\"kw760\">conj</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>cexp<span class=\"br0\">(</span>z<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>\n</li><li> If <code>z</code> is <code>±0+0i</code>, the result is <code>1+0i</code>\n</li><li> If <code>z</code> is <code>x+∞i</code> (for any finite x), the result is <code>NaN+NaNi</code> and <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/fenv/FE_exceptions\">FE_INVALID</a></span> is raised.\n</li><li> If <code>z</code> is <code>x+NaNi</code> (for any finite x), the result is <code>NaN+NaNi</code> and <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/fenv/FE_exceptions\">FE_INVALID</a></span> may be raised.\n</li><li> If <code>z</code> is <code>+∞+0i</code>, the result is <code>+∞+0i</code>\n</li><li> If <code>z</code> is <code>-∞+yi</code> (for any finite y), the result is <code>+0cis(y)</code>\n</li><li> If <code>z</code> is <code>+∞+yi</code> (for any finite nonzero y), the result is <code>+∞cis(y)</code>\n</li><li> If <code>z</code> is <code>-∞+∞i</code>, the result is <code>±0±0i</code> (signs are unspecified)\n</li><li> If <code>z</code> is <code>+∞+∞i</code>, the result is <code>±∞+NaNi</code> and <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/fenv/FE_exceptions\">FE_INVALID</a></span> is raised (the sign of the real part is unspecified)\n</li><li> If <code>z</code> is <code>-∞+NaNi</code>, the result is <code>±0±0i</code> (signs are unspecified)\n</li><li> If <code>z</code> is <code>+∞+NaNi</code>, the result is <code>±∞+NaNi</code> (the sign of the real part is unspecified)\n</li><li> If <code>z</code> is <code>NaN+0i</code>, the result is <code>NaN+0i</code>\n</li><li> If <code>z</code> is <code>NaN+yi</code> (for any nonzero y), the result is <code>NaN+NaNi</code> and <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/fenv/FE_exceptions\">FE_INVALID</a></span> may be raised\n</li><li> If <code>z</code> is <code>NaN+NaNi</code>, the result is <code>NaN+NaNi</code>\n</li></ul>\n<p>where <span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"\\small{\\rm cis}(y)\">cis(y)</span> is <span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"\\small \\cos(y)+{\\rm i}\\sin(y)\">cos(y) + i sin(y)</span>\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>The complex exponential function <span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"\\small e^z\">e<span class=\"t-su\">z<br></span></span> for <span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"\\small z = x + {\\rm i}y\">z = x+iy</span> equals <span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"\\small e^x {\\rm cis}(y)\">e<span class=\"t-su\">x<br></span> cis(y)</span>, or, <span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"\\small e^x (\\cos(y)+{\\rm i}\\sin(y))\">e<span class=\"t-su\">x<br></span> (cos(y) + i sin(y))</span>\n</p><p>The exponential function is an <i>entire function</i> in the complex plane and has no branch cuts.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"c\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;math.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;complex.h&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> PI <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/math/acos\"><span class=\"kw673\">acos</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu0\">1</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/complex\"><span class=\"kw743\">complex</span></a> z <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> cexp<span class=\"br0\">(</span>I <span class=\"sy2\">*</span> PI<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// Euler's formula</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw848\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"exp(i*pi) =&nbsp;%.1f%+.1fi<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>, <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/creal\"><span class=\"kw754\">creal</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z<span class=\"br0\">)</span>, <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/cimag\"><span class=\"kw751\">cimag</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>exp(i*pi) = -1.0+0.0i</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"References\">References</h3>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-11\">\n<ul><li> C11 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:2011): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.3.7.1 The cexp functions (p: 194)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.25 Type-generic math &lt;tgmath.h&gt; (p: 373-375)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> G.6.3.1 The cexp functions (p: 543)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> G.7 Type-generic math &lt;tgmath.h&gt; (p: 545)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-c99\">\n<ul><li> C99 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:1999): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.3.7.1 The cexp functions (p: 176)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.22 Type-generic math &lt;tgmath.h&gt; (p: 335-337)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> G.6.3.1 The cexp functions (p: 478)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> G.7 Type-generic math &lt;tgmath.h&gt; (p: 480)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/clog\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>clog</span><span>clogf</span><span>clogl</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   computes the complex natural logarithm <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/math/exp\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>exp</span><span>expf</span><span>expl</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   computes <i>e</i> raised to the given power (<span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"{\\small e^x}\">e<sup>x</sup></span>)  <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <div class=\"t-dsc-see\"><span><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/exp\">C++ documentation</a></span> for <span class=\"t-dsc-see-tt\"><span>exp</span></span></div>\n</td></tr>\n</table></div>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Error handling and special values","id":"Error_handling_and_special_values"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"References","id":"References"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C reference"},{"path":"numeric","title":"Numerics"},{"path":"numeric/complex","title":"Complex number arithmetic"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"cexpf, cexp, cexpl","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"4 declarations. Computes the complex base-e exponential of z."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"z"},{"label":"Return value","note":"If no errors occur, e raised to the power of z, ez is returned."},{"label":"Error handling and special values","note":"Errors are reported consistent with math_errhandling."},{"label":"Notes","note":"The complex exponential function ez for z = x+iy equals ex cis(y), or, ex (cos(y) + i sin(y))"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"clog, clogf, clogl","note":"computes the complex natural logarithm"},{"label":"exp, expf, expl","note":"computes e raised to the given power (ex)"}]}]},"standards":["C99"],"wordCount":477,"codeBlockCount":2}
